WEBVTT

00:01:34.130 --> 00:01:39.190
<b>8. A Knight's Vow</b>

00:01:57.200 --> 00:01:59.360
The bleeding won't stop.

00:01:59.940 --> 00:02:02.430
Yukimaru... isn't gonna die, is he?

00:02:02.530 --> 00:02:05.900
Don't even <i>think</i> stuff like that!
No way is Yukimaru gonna die!

00:02:06.000 --> 00:02:08.370
- Right, Tsubaki?
- Y-Yeah...

00:02:20.790 --> 00:02:22.890
We have to get the bullet out
and stop the bleeding!

00:02:23.990 --> 00:02:26.810
- What's the nearest port?
- Saint-Malo.

00:02:26.910 --> 00:02:29.510
That would put us on the sea lane
that navies use, though.

00:02:30.250 --> 00:02:33.720
It's a little far, but Chaouen
would let us travel on the surface.

00:02:33.820 --> 00:02:35.650
We know a doctor there, too.

00:02:36.250 --> 00:02:37.620
- Kaede!
- Yessir!

00:02:37.720 --> 00:02:41.650
- Tell Makaba and Enju to set course for Chaouen!
- Aye aye!

00:02:49.380 --> 00:02:50.520
Yukimaru...

00:03:19.990 --> 00:03:22.450
Kei's team didn't
get there in time?

00:03:22.550 --> 00:03:24.130
I heard they were wiped out.

00:03:24.230 --> 00:03:26.570
Every last person
aboard the <i>Hope...</i>

00:03:27.450 --> 00:03:30.300
They say that Yukimaru
was the only survivor.

00:03:30.400 --> 00:03:32.410
Even Lord Franz...

00:03:39.040 --> 00:03:42.650
There's nothing you can do for him
by standing there. Go home and rest.

00:04:31.300 --> 00:04:32.950
How is Yukimaru?

00:04:33.050 --> 00:04:34.960
How did you prevent the wound
from festering?

00:04:35.060 --> 00:04:36.480
Oh, um...

00:04:36.870 --> 00:04:38.670
We used tobacco leaves.

00:04:38.770 --> 00:04:40.730
Oh, that explains it.

00:04:41.180 --> 00:04:43.800
If festering had set in,
he might have died.

00:04:43.900 --> 00:04:45.740
That was the proper treatment.

00:04:46.360 --> 00:04:47.930
You don't need to worry.

00:04:48.030 --> 00:04:51.690
All he needs now
is time to recuperate.

00:04:52.750 --> 00:04:55.770
- So Yukimaru is--
- Yes, he'll be fine.

00:04:55.870 --> 00:04:57.420
What a relief!

00:04:58.100 --> 00:05:01.030
- Awesome!
- That's our Yukimaru!

00:05:01.130 --> 00:05:04.070
<i>You</i> said that Yukimaru
was gonna die!

00:05:04.170 --> 00:05:07.040
- Come on, you two.
- It was Fena.

00:05:04.170 --> 00:05:07.040
Say what?! <i>You</i> were saying that!

00:05:08.230 --> 00:05:10.890
Fena was the one
who saved Yukimaru's life.

00:05:13.140 --> 00:05:15.890
Fena kept Yukimaru safe, didn't she?

00:05:16.470 --> 00:05:18.400
I guess she did at that.

00:05:21.030 --> 00:05:24.770
- What a relief! I was so worried!
- What a relief! I was so worried!

00:05:25.680 --> 00:05:27.660
Don't be so quick
to sing her praises.

00:05:29.300 --> 00:05:31.160
You have this backwards.

00:05:31.950 --> 00:05:33.220
It was Fena

00:05:33.320 --> 00:05:35.540
who forced him into that situation
in the first place.

00:05:35.770 --> 00:05:36.890
What do you mean, <i>forced</i> him?!

00:05:37.000 --> 00:05:39.420
Come on, what happened to him
wasn't Fena's fault!

00:05:39.800 --> 00:05:42.990
- They're right, if those pirates hadn't--
- Isn't the fact that you're thinking that way

00:05:43.090 --> 00:05:46.040
proof that you've all
fallen under her spell?

00:05:47.080 --> 00:05:49.220
The spell of that witch, Fena.

00:05:59.010 --> 00:06:00.690
What do you mean by that?

00:06:01.590 --> 00:06:03.570
"That witch"?

00:06:05.470 --> 00:06:06.840
It's nothing.

00:06:06.940 --> 00:06:08.320
Shitan.

00:06:09.000 --> 00:06:10.320
Tell us everything.

00:06:10.820 --> 00:06:13.820
This isn't something that
you should shoulder alone.

00:06:20.790 --> 00:06:22.500
With Franz now dead,

00:06:22.600 --> 00:06:26.960
the only clues left to us
are Fena Houtman's memories.

00:06:28.170 --> 00:06:30.610
However, she comes from
a line of witches.

00:06:31.900 --> 00:06:32.900
Witches?

00:06:33.000 --> 00:06:36.460
She corrupts men, leads them astray,
and brings them low.

00:06:37.150 --> 00:06:39.120
It was true of her mother.

00:06:39.220 --> 00:06:42.530
I know a man who was
driven mad by her charms.

00:06:42.630 --> 00:06:45.080
What would you have me do?

00:06:45.180 --> 00:06:47.110
Watch Yukimaru closely.

00:06:47.790 --> 00:06:51.110
If Yukimaru should ever appear
to have fallen under her sway,

00:06:52.060 --> 00:06:52.940
...strike.

00:06:57.800 --> 00:07:00.330
Even under your orders, Priest,

00:07:01.450 --> 00:07:04.350
I could never kill Yukimaru.

00:07:04.450 --> 00:07:05.840
Yes, I know.

00:07:06.480 --> 00:07:08.340
The one I am telling you strike down

00:07:08.660 --> 00:07:10.340
is not Yukimaru.

00:07:11.640 --> 00:07:14.040
But rather the witch.

00:07:15.250 --> 00:07:16.640
That's...

00:07:17.510 --> 00:07:19.770
...what you think of me?

00:07:22.710 --> 00:07:23.770
Shitan!

00:07:24.210 --> 00:07:25.770
- Shitan, I'm not--
- It's the truth.

00:07:26.750 --> 00:07:29.360
The others chose you
over the island.

00:07:29.460 --> 00:07:30.530
Look, Shitan!

00:07:30.990 --> 00:07:32.630
- We all made our own choice--
- As a result,

00:07:32.730 --> 00:07:34.530
now we're all hunted men.

00:07:36.630 --> 00:07:40.530
We spent years building up
their trust in us!

00:07:40.620 --> 00:07:42.130
At the risk of our lives!

00:07:42.630 --> 00:07:46.040
- And in the span of a few short weeks, you--
- Shitan!

00:07:48.000 --> 00:07:50.050
Shitan, what's gotten into you?

00:07:50.340 --> 00:07:54.360
Everything we've done was of our own
free will. Not because of Fena!

00:07:54.460 --> 00:07:56.050
Stop taking things out on her!

00:07:56.870 --> 00:07:59.060
Taking things out... on her?

00:07:59.410 --> 00:08:03.060
Yeah! All you're doing
is lashing out at Fena!

00:08:04.190 --> 00:08:06.880
Look, Shitan.
Think things through, and you'll see--

00:08:11.760 --> 00:08:14.200
Ten years ago,
and now once again.

00:08:14.810 --> 00:08:16.950
He's hurt...

00:08:17.610 --> 00:08:19.000
...because of you.

00:08:46.100 --> 00:08:48.410
- Oh, wow!
- <i>Ippon!</i>

00:08:48.510 --> 00:08:51.350
- You won again, Yukimaru!
- You're awesome!

00:08:53.280 --> 00:08:54.950
- Yukimaru.
- Yes?

00:08:55.450 --> 00:08:57.660
That strike was well executed.

00:08:58.010 --> 00:08:59.510
Thank you.

00:09:00.080 --> 00:09:04.210
But not all swordsmen you will face on
the battlefield will be as weak as this one.

00:09:04.310 --> 00:09:07.790
- Take that lesson to heart.
- I will.

00:09:07.890 --> 00:09:09.730
You may go rest.

00:09:19.470 --> 00:09:20.930
How pathetic.

00:09:37.540 --> 00:09:39.820
No, not those.

00:09:40.940 --> 00:09:42.580
Those are rejects.

00:09:42.940 --> 00:09:47.330
They're so stiff that it's impossible
to tell where the arrow will go.

00:09:48.040 --> 00:09:51.330
Oh. Rejects, huh?

00:09:52.910 --> 00:09:54.840
Just like me, then.

00:09:55.850 --> 00:09:58.840
Makaba. Would you mind
if I tried one out?

00:10:14.750 --> 00:10:17.250
So, how is that bow
of Makaba's?

00:10:18.270 --> 00:10:20.770
Tricky. The arrows go wide.

00:10:22.680 --> 00:10:26.150
They never go where I'm aiming at.
It doesn't listen to me.

00:10:26.250 --> 00:10:29.120
Then why don't you listen to <i>it?</i>

00:10:30.680 --> 00:10:32.630
Aim your shot

00:10:32.840 --> 00:10:34.750
where the arrow
wants to go.

00:10:35.080 --> 00:10:36.730
Listen to <i>it.</i>

00:10:43.650 --> 00:10:45.640
Aim where the arrow
wants to go...

00:10:47.320 --> 00:10:50.850
<i>Don't let the target lead you astray...</i>

00:10:57.970 --> 00:10:59.360
I hit it!

00:11:00.560 --> 00:11:02.340
You're good at that, Shitan.

00:11:03.450 --> 00:11:05.940
I haven't mastered it, but I will.

00:11:24.410 --> 00:11:25.760
Brule?

00:11:26.600 --> 00:11:28.890
Brule! Good job!

00:11:36.990 --> 00:11:38.900
I finally found you!

00:11:39.480 --> 00:11:40.670
Fena?

00:11:44.560 --> 00:11:46.030
- Shitan, I--
- Go away.

00:11:48.150 --> 00:11:51.660
- The others filled me in on--
- Didn't you hear me?

00:11:53.650 --> 00:11:55.000
Go away.

00:11:56.210 --> 00:11:58.150
If they told you,
then it should be clear to you.

00:11:58.250 --> 00:12:00.170
- My orders are to kill you.
- Shitan.

00:12:01.350 --> 00:12:03.130
You would never do that.

00:12:04.870 --> 00:12:07.930
You taught me how to use a bow.

00:12:08.550 --> 00:12:11.110
I'm twice as bad at learning stuff
as anyone else,

00:12:11.210 --> 00:12:13.440
but you tried your hardest
to teach me.

00:12:14.150 --> 00:12:15.440
And besides!

00:12:15.960 --> 00:12:18.440
I still can't hit
the broad side of a barn!

00:12:18.800 --> 00:12:19.440
Huh?

00:12:19.740 --> 00:12:22.090
You heard me! I still can't
shoot worth a darn!

00:12:22.190 --> 00:12:26.300
If you don't keep teaching me,
I don't think I'll ever hit anything!

00:12:25.060 --> 00:12:26.300
Now wait just a minute...

00:12:26.400 --> 00:12:30.680
Is that what you want? If your student is that bad,
it's <i>you</i> who should feel ashamed!

00:12:30.780 --> 00:12:32.450
- What are you babbling around?
- What I'm saying...

00:12:33.270 --> 00:12:35.270
...is that I want to
spend my life traveling!

00:12:36.320 --> 00:12:38.050
With Yukimaru and you!

00:12:38.150 --> 00:12:40.030
And Karin and the twins!

00:12:40.130 --> 00:12:42.280
And Tsubaki and Makaba.
With all of you.

00:12:43.720 --> 00:12:46.220
Forever. And ever.

00:12:47.500 --> 00:12:48.570
Fena...

00:12:48.670 --> 00:12:49.450
And besides!

00:12:49.450 --> 00:12:53.850
If I <i>were</i> a witch, I'd use my magic
to use this bow like a pro!

00:12:54.470 --> 00:12:55.170
Huh?

00:12:55.450 --> 00:12:58.330
I don't fly on a broomstick!
I don't have a black cat!

00:12:58.430 --> 00:13:00.310
I just have a big, white dog!

00:13:00.410 --> 00:13:04.000
I keep getting smacked on the head!
I've even been tossed into the ocean!

00:13:04.100 --> 00:13:06.170
I dumb! I'm not a morning person!
I'm not in shape!

00:13:06.270 --> 00:13:08.000
I can't use a single weapon!

00:13:08.100 --> 00:13:10.520
I don't have a crystal ball!
I can't predict the future!

00:13:10.620 --> 00:13:13.370
You could search the world from top to bottom
and not find a single witch like...

00:13:14.530 --> 00:13:15.870
...me?

00:13:17.450 --> 00:13:18.880
Shitan?

00:13:20.830 --> 00:13:22.880
Shitan? What are you doing?

00:13:29.500 --> 00:13:32.050
Um, Shitan?

00:13:37.260 --> 00:13:41.400
I think I understand how you felt when
you whacked her all those times, Yukimaru...

00:13:45.090 --> 00:13:46.230
Get a move on.

00:13:49.320 --> 00:13:51.190
- Shitan?
- Let's head back.

00:13:52.840 --> 00:13:55.780
We'll set out again
as soon as Yukimaru wakes up.

00:13:57.870 --> 00:14:00.000
Let's go together.

00:14:30.010 --> 00:14:33.350
I don't... have any feeling
in my legs.

00:14:35.020 --> 00:14:35.720
Fena!

00:14:57.620 --> 00:14:58.540
Fena.

00:14:59.370 --> 00:15:00.620
Fena.

00:15:03.340 --> 00:15:04.380
Fena.

00:15:04.880 --> 00:15:05.920
Fena!

00:15:15.640 --> 00:15:16.890
Ow!

00:15:24.940 --> 00:15:26.940
That was mean,
why'd you do that?!

00:15:27.070 --> 00:15:30.860
I thought I had lost my legs.
I was scared for a second.

00:15:30.990 --> 00:15:32.320
Sorry.

00:15:33.490 --> 00:15:34.910
Has Shitan...

00:15:35.740 --> 00:15:37.080
...come around yet?

00:15:40.460 --> 00:15:42.290
I can't say for sure,

00:15:42.370 --> 00:15:44.290
but he said we'd
all go together.

00:15:44.960 --> 00:15:47.250
Where has he been
since yesterday?

00:15:47.340 --> 00:15:49.630
The others have gone back
to the ship,

00:15:49.720 --> 00:15:52.550
but Shitan and the doctor went out
to the entertainment district.

00:15:52.630 --> 00:15:55.430
- He said he knew a bar with pretty--
- He's fine, then.

00:15:56.010 --> 00:15:56.930
He is?

00:15:57.890 --> 00:15:59.930
You don't need to worry.

00:16:02.020 --> 00:16:03.940
More importantly...

00:16:05.020 --> 00:16:07.020
why were you aboard
that navy ship?

00:16:07.480 --> 00:16:10.940
Oh. It's a... long story.

00:16:11.900 --> 00:16:15.450
Will you tell me about it?
If you can.

00:16:46.440 --> 00:16:48.520
I see.

00:16:49.110 --> 00:16:53.240
So much has happened that it feels
like my head is about to burst.

00:16:55.200 --> 00:16:57.280
Look, I'm sorry.

00:16:58.200 --> 00:16:59.790
Why are you apologizing?

00:17:00.330 --> 00:17:04.080
Yesterday, I was acting all upbeat
when I talked to Shitan.

00:17:04.460 --> 00:17:06.790
But the truth is, I'm not.

00:17:08.000 --> 00:17:11.300
I started out as Fena Houtman.

00:17:12.210 --> 00:17:15.300
And then I became
Fena of Shangri-La,

00:17:15.380 --> 00:17:17.800
and after that, I was called
the White Marginal.

00:17:18.680 --> 00:17:22.310
And now people call me "Princess"
or a witch.

00:17:23.520 --> 00:17:27.440
Who the heck am I?

00:17:29.610 --> 00:17:33.440
It's possible that you'll only
find that answer at that place.

00:17:35.490 --> 00:17:38.450
At the place I promised Franz
I would take you.

00:17:39.280 --> 00:17:40.450
Eden.

00:17:44.710 --> 00:17:47.960
I want to go there.
But at the same time, I don't.

00:17:51.340 --> 00:17:52.960
A thought hit me.

00:17:53.550 --> 00:17:57.800
Maybe I could keep on traveling
with you guys.

00:17:58.930 --> 00:18:02.640
Going around to various islands
and visiting parts unknown.

00:18:03.640 --> 00:18:06.850
And having fun every day.

00:18:08.060 --> 00:18:11.690
If I did that, I could stay
who I am right now.

00:18:12.610 --> 00:18:16.610
Then nothing would have to change.

00:18:17.860 --> 00:18:21.120
Are you afraid
of moving forward now?

00:18:22.330 --> 00:18:24.120
I guess I might be.

00:18:25.700 --> 00:18:28.080
I'm sorry.
I'm really not helping things.

00:18:28.210 --> 00:18:29.880
Either way, it's all right.

00:18:31.250 --> 00:18:33.880
Wherever you want to go,
I'll go with you.

00:18:34.000 --> 00:18:36.510
Wherever you stop,
I'll stop too.

00:18:37.760 --> 00:18:40.090
Like the raicho birds
on the island.

00:18:42.180 --> 00:18:43.510
When I was little,

00:18:44.100 --> 00:18:47.020
my father told me something
that a great man once said.

00:18:48.060 --> 00:18:52.310
"In this fleeting life, there are two
moments of joy above all others.

00:18:52.820 --> 00:18:56.150
When we are born into this world
and take our first breath.

00:18:56.650 --> 00:18:57.530
And...

00:18:58.320 --> 00:19:00.910
...when we learn what we
were put on this earth to do."

00:19:04.330 --> 00:19:06.330
I don't know what they will be,

00:19:07.000 --> 00:19:10.920
but I do think that the answers you seek
can be found only there.

00:19:11.630 --> 00:19:15.550
The answer to who you are.
And...

00:19:17.170 --> 00:19:20.050
...the answer to why
you and I met.

00:19:21.680 --> 00:19:25.060
I'll keep protecting you.
I'll protect you with all that I have.

00:19:25.970 --> 00:19:27.220
Yukimaru...

00:19:28.730 --> 00:19:31.310
To make sure the others won't
be put in danger again,

00:19:31.440 --> 00:19:33.560
I'll strive to become
even stronger.

00:19:35.320 --> 00:19:36.440
Fena.

00:19:38.240 --> 00:19:39.950
Let's go together.

00:19:41.610 --> 00:19:42.950
Yukimaru!

00:19:43.240 --> 00:19:44.950
Are you okay?
Does something hurt?

00:19:56.750 --> 00:19:59.050
Y-Yukimaru? What's the matter?

00:19:59.550 --> 00:20:01.470
- Fena.
- Y-Yes?

00:20:02.090 --> 00:20:06.470
No matter what happens,
I swear I will always keep you safe.

00:20:10.980 --> 00:20:12.600
My hand...

00:20:13.400 --> 00:20:15.110
...will never again...

00:20:16.730 --> 00:20:18.730
...let go of yours.

00:20:47.720 --> 00:20:50.890
It's gotten chilly.
Let's go back inside.

00:21:49.700 --> 00:21:53.080
Helena. We will meet again soon.

00:21:54.540 --> 00:21:55.800
It won't be long.
